#
# PAM service `abyss`: the authenticator behind the lock screen and the login
# window (desktop/docs/PHASE16.md, P16.1). Asked by abyss-loginwindow, as root,
# about the account of whoever is calling.
#
# Its own stack — NOT `include login`. login's stack begins with pam_self,
# which passes whenever the caller is the target user; the caller here is the
# root daemon, so a root session's screen would unlock with no password.
# nullok, as `system` has it: an account with no password (the live medium's)
# can still unlock its own screen.
#
auth		required	pam_unix.so		no_warn try_first_pass nullok
account		required	pam_unix.so
